;; The reviews of C++'s samples' and runtime's golden files (c-cpp-golden, the user's decision of 2026-11-20: reviewed golden files
;; for C++'s sample prints; test/cpp/selfref.ae). Beside each program of test/cpp/samples and test/cpp/runtime/samples: NAME.expect,
;; its standard output byte for byte (empty when it prints nothing); NAME.cpp.expectrc, its exit status when not 0 (mir's
;; NAME.c.expectrc, C's run corpora); NAME.expect-stderr, its standard error when it writes one. Each written from the program's
;; source and C++23 before it was compared with anything, then checked against g++ 15.2's recorded run (test/cpp/ref-gxx15.edn's
;; status and SHA-256s: 15 of 15 met at the first writing, an agreement found, not used). A golden file is a verdict only with its
;; review here, and a review only with its golden file (cpp.selfref's ref fails otherwise).
;; :basis what fixes the output: :src the program's own code under C++23's semantics; :abi the target's ABI (the Itanium C++ ABI's
;; type names, the x86-64 psABI's layout, Linux's SIGABRT 6 reported as status 134 by the check's harness, 128 + the signal);
;; :lib the target's library, libstdc++ 15.2 as its source in the pinned gcc tarball says (messages, the verbose terminate handler:
;; libsupc++/vterminate.cc); :gnu GCC's documented attributes. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "samples/auto.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "main returns n::id<int>(x) 1 + ::n::g 0 (static storage, zero-initialized) + l(2) (a + x) 3 + a[1] 2 + (int)u 3 + static_cast<int>(2.5) 2 (truncated, [conv.fpint]) = 11; nothing printed"}
 {:id "samples/bitfields.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "a value stored into a bit-field of width N is reduced modulo 2^N ([class.bit], [conv.integral]): s24.a 5 + 0xfffffe = 0x1000003 mod 2^24 = 3, c 2: \"3 2\"; s40.a (40 bits of unsigned long, wider than int: no promotion) 0xffffffffff + 2 mod 2^40 = 1, b 7, c 9: \"1 7 9\"; s48.a -5 - 1 = -6, n 0xbeef: \"-6 beef\"; s56.a 0x11223344556677 ^ 0xffffffffffffff = 0xeeddccbbaa9988, z 0x88: \"eeddccbbaa9988 88\"; p17.a 0x1ffff + 1 mod 2^17 = 0, b 0x5555 << 1 = 0xaaaa mod 2^15 = 0x2aaa: \"0 2aaa\"; main falls off its end: 0"}
 {:id "samples/classes.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "if (int y = 2; y > 1) return 1: status 1, after the try that catches its own int; nothing printed (D's leak is not observable)"}
 {:id "samples/coroutine.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "count(3) suspends at its initial suspend; each resume runs to the next co_yield (0, 1, 2), added while the handle is not done; the fourth resume ends the loop, return_void, final_suspend leaves it done: 0 + 1 + 2 = 3; nothing printed"}
 {:id "samples/io.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "{3, 1, 2} sorted ascending, each element then '\\n': \"1\", \"2\", \"3\"; main returns 0"}
 {:id "samples/p1-first.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "f(): S's constructor and destructor print nothing, the int thrown is caught inside f, l(2) = twice(2) 4 + W<int>{1}.get() 1 = 5; v.size() 2: 7; nothing printed"}
 {:id "samples/vexing.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "U u(T()) declares a function (the most vexing parse, [dcl.ambig.res]), U w((T())) constructs a U; main falls off its end: 0; nothing printed"}
 {:id "runtime/atomics.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "every value is fixed by the atomics' and the static's guarantees, not by the threads' timing: counter 4 x 100000 fetch_add(1) less the fetch_sub(id)s 0+1+2+3 = 399994; max: each thread's compare-exchange loop raises maxv to its largest i, 99999; flags: each thread sets bit id, 15; inits: Slow's constructor runs once ([stmt.dcl]/3: a concurrent initialization waits for the first), 1; sums: local_static() 42 plus (*copy)[0] = 1 at the 100 values of i divisible by 1000, 142 for each thread; use_count: the threads' copies are destroyed before join returns, the weak_ptr does not count, 1, expired 0; after reset expired 1"}
 {:id "runtime/ctor-throw.cpp" :basis [:src :gnu :lib :abi]
  :why "the initializer of a (init_priority 200) runs before later (constructor 300: GCC's documented priorities, the lower first), writes \"A\" to stderr and throws runtime_error; an exception leaving a non-local static's initialization calls std::terminate ([except.terminate]), so neither later nor main runs; the default handler, libstdc++'s __verbose_terminate_handler (libsupc++/vterminate.cc), writes \"terminate called after throwing an instance of '\" the demangled type (St13runtime_error: std::runtime_error) \"'\", then \"  what():  \" and what(), and calls abort: status 134; stdout empty"}
 {:id "runtime/deferred.cpp" :basis [:src :abi]
  :why "sum(5, 1..5) through vsum's va_list: 15; mix(2, ...): 1.5 + 7 + (1*10 + 2) + 9 + 'A' 65 = 94.5 and 2.5 + 8 + 34 + 11 + 'B' 66 = 121.5, 216 by %g; fwd: k 42 read inline, vsnprintf of \"%d-%s\" on the rest (7, \"x\"): \"[42 7-x]\"; f 1.5 stored 3.5, exchange gives o 3.5 (f 4), fetch_add gives a 4 (f 4.5); d exchange gives e 2.25 (d 8.5), fetch_sub 1.25 leaves 7.25, exp 7.25, compare_exchange_strong succeeds (ok 1, d 1): \"3.5 4 4.5 | 2.25 7.25 1 1\"; LD under the x86-64 psABI (long double 16 bytes aligned 16: c at 0, v at 16, tail at 32, size 48), 1.5 + (-0.25 * 4) = 0.50, pr.second 7, 'a' 'b': \"48 16 0.50 7 ab\"; (1.5 - 2i) * 2 = (3, -4): \"3.00 -4.00\"; hash<long double> of 0.0 and -0.0, equal values, are equal ([unord.hash]): 1; status 0"}
 {:id "runtime/hello.cpp" :basis [:src :lib :abi]
  :why "\"hello world\"; {5,3,9,1,7} sorted, each with a space: \"1 3 5 7 9 \"; \"abc\" + to_string(42), size 5: \"abc42 5\"; the map in key order one, three, two; v.at(10) throws out_of_range: \"caught out_of_range\"; \"caught boom\"; b->name() \"Derived\", typeid(*b).name() the Itanium ABI's mangled \"7Derived\", the dynamic_cast's bool printed as 1; stoi(\"x\") throws invalid_argument whose what() is the function's name, \"stoi\" (libstdc++'s __stoa, ext/string_conversions.h); 3.25 and 1e10 at the default precision 6 (%g): \"3.25 1e+10\", 255 in hex \"ff\"; the rethrown 7; stderr \"to stderr\"; status 0"}
 {:id "runtime/library.cpp" :basis [:src :lib :abi]
  :why "Counter's constructor once (\"Counter()\"), its n 3 at the third call: \"counter 3\"; p[3] 4; new of an alignas(64) type is 64-aligned: \"aligned 0\"; reserve beyond max_size throws length_error; operator new of 2^63 - 1 bytes cannot succeed on the target: bad_alloc, what() \"std::bad_alloc\" (libsupc++/bad_alloc.cc); num_put<char, char*> is not in the classic locale: bad_cast; get<double> of a variant holding int: \"std::get: wrong index for variant\" (<variant>'s reasons); an empty function: \"bad_function_call\" (src/c++11/functional.cc); any_cast<float> of an int: \"bad any_cast\" (<any>); the streambuf's overflow throws, the stream sets badbit and rethrows the original under exceptions(badbit) ([ostream.formatted.reqmts]): \"callback overflow\"; \"abc\" >> int sets failbit under exceptions(failbit): \"ios_base::failure\"; throw_with_nested's outer \"outer\", its nested int \"nested 1\"; C* as B* yes, as the unrelated X no, typeid C: \"1 0 1\"; the Itanium ABI's names \"i PKc St6vectorIiSaIiEE\"; the default locale \"C\"; \"1.5 -7 true\"; to_chars' shortest round trip of the double nearest pi, \"3.141592653589793\", read back and printed by %.15g, \"3.14159265358979\"; format's \"    ab|ff|2.5\"; status 0"}
 {:id "runtime/thread-throw.cpp" :basis [:src :lib :abi]
  :why "\"main\" then the thread's \"thread\" on stderr; the exception leaving the thread's callable calls std::terminate ([thread.thread.constr]), with the exception current (an implicit handler, [except.handle]/7): the verbose handler's two lines for std::runtime_error, what() \"from a thread\", then abort: status 134; \"joined\" never written; stdout empty"}
 {:id "runtime/threads.cpp" :basis [:src]
  :why "each work(id) over i < 20000: i % 4 == id throws runtime_error \"tID\", caught +1, 5000 times; otherwise i % 5 == 0 throws i, caught +2: the 4000 multiples of 5 less the 1000 also == id mod 4, 3000 times; 5000 + 6000 = 11000 in each thread, independent of the scheduling; all > 0: status 0"}
 {:id "runtime/uncaught.cpp" :basis [:src :lib :abi]
  :why "puts \"before\" and flushes stdout; f throws logic_error(\"no handler\") and no handler matches: std::terminate ([except.handle]/9), the verbose handler's lines for std::logic_error and what() \"no handler\", then abort: status 134; \"not reached\" never written"}]
